  "notes": "{除草|じょそう} means weeding or removing unwanted plants. A compound of {除|じょ} (remove) + {草|そう} (grass/weeds).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {除草|じょそう}する: to weed\n- {除草|じょそう}{剤|ざい}: herbicide, weed killer\n- {除草|じょそう}{作業|さぎょう}: weeding work\n- {除草|じょそう}{機|き}: weed trimmer, mower\n\nUSAGE:\nA practical term used in gardening, agriculture, and property maintenance. Common in spring and summer when weeds grow rapidly.\n\nHOMOPHONES (IMPORTANT):\n- {除草|じょそう}: weeding (this entry)\n- {助走|じょそう}: run-up, approach run (sports)\n- {女装|じょそう}: dressing as a woman, cross-dressing\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {草|くさ}むしり: pulling weeds by hand (casual, everyday)\n- {草刈|くさか}り: mowing grass/weeds",
